<i>Genius Chef</i>

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.420
No way in through that window.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:49.120
But the door's the only other exit, and it was locked.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.520
Which means this is another locked room.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.700
Two headless corpses, and two locked rooms.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.960
A second headless corpse, and a second locked room.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:03.540
No sign of the head.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:09.420
Like with Kanami, this could not be suicide, or accidental.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.640
Well. This certainly changes everything.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.860
Shall we regroup in the dining room?

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:23.280
Hikari, lock this room again, please.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.280
It changes everything, hunh?

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.280
So now we have a murder sequence.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:33.760
A murder sequence...

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:39.380
I'd suggested keeping Akane here to prevent that happening.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.840
Creating a stalemate?

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:51.800
As if I could ever stop the killer from acting.
The nerve. The audacity. The conceit.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:55.340
You protected me.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:05:00.360
Mushanokoji

00:04:55.350 --> 00:05:00.360
Baka Ichi

00:04:55.860 --> 00:05:00.360
I could have suggested it myself, but I figured that was a bad idea.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:04.940
When you suggested it for me, I was grateful.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.700
I should put that gratitude in words.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:14.580
Ilia's favorite -- Aikawa, was it?

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:20.440
Maintaining the status quo till this Aikawa
gets here seemed like the best plan.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.520
Would she say the same now?

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:27.120
Nonsense. In the end.

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:38.080
Ii-chan, come on!

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.680
We're keeping Ilia waiting.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.680
Everyone else is already there.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:47.840
Right.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.950
1st Floor, Dining Room

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:07.220
Around two in the morning...

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:08.380
1st Floor, Chiga Hikari's Room

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.640
Sonoyama called my room.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:17.520
She asked me to bring her a book she had left in her room.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:23.020
So...she was still alive at the time, yes?

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.580
She still had a head?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.300
Yes. She was alive at the time.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.280
Baka Ichi

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:35.140
Akane's body had been discovered around nine thirty this morning.

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:41.660
Akane always woke up early, and took breakfast at the exact same time.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:43.000
When they didn't hear from her,

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:46.170
1st Floor, Storeroom, Exterior

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.900
Hikari thought it was odd...and found her.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:52.700
OK...then shall we begin with alibis again?

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.100
This time I have no alibi.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:07:03.180
Hikari came to our room between ten and eleven.
After that, Kunagisa and I both went to bed.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:08.780
Well, if you were asleep, you couldn't have
known if the other one snuck out of the room.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.700
Well, it definitely wasn't me.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:15.200
The storeroom is on the first floor!

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:18.420
I can't go down stairs alone.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:25.420
That's why I brought Ii-chan with me.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:28.400
This was a rule.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:38.860
Not a characteristic or an idiosyncrasy or a foible but
a firm, clear, inflexible rule built into the fabric of her mind.

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:40.700
You...can't?

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:46.940
Have you ever seen me climbing the stairs alone? Since I arrived here?

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:51.200
But there's no way for us to verify this, is there?

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:53.440
She has a certificate from her doctor.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:57.640
It's a psychogenic reaction; a type of psychological impairment.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:02.460
I think that will be enough to establish Kunagisa's alibi.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.580
Then...Himena?

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:09.720
I was in my room, drinking all night.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.880
With my handsome gentleman friend here.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.360
Is that right, Sakaki?

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.460
I'm hardly a gentleman, but otherwise, yes.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:21.900
Around one AM...I just couldn't sleep.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.480
I went to the living room. Himena was there.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:24.480
1st Floor, Living Room

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:30.000
She asked me to join her, we went to her room...and then it was morning.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:33.400
I was asleep in my room the whole time.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:35.620
I have no alibi.

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:45.120
I woke up at six, and began making breakfast...from that
point on, Hikari helped a bit, so she can speak for me, I guess.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:51.960
Then...Hikari?

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:57.100
Like I said, I brought a book to Sonoyama at two.

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:03.180
Then I went back to sleep. Until I woke up this morning, I have no alibi.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:04.380
Oh.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:09.020
I suppose I should speak for myself here.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:15.480
I was talking to Rei in my room all night.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.660
Isn't that right, Rei?

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:24.280
We went to bed at noon yesterday, so
were hardly ready for sleep in the evening.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:31.440
By the time our conversation ended, it was morning.
There seemed little point in sleeping at that point, and, well...

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:33.920
We came to breakfast.

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:38.000
I believe that qualifies as an alibi, yes?

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:40.640
Yes, I believe it does.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:44.300
Akari, Teruko...when did you get back?

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.760
Around nine.

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:48.920
Nine...?

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:55.220
Then I believe we can consider that their alibi.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:56.900
Which means...

00:09:58.320 --> 00:09:59.680
The ones with alibis...

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:01.880
Sakaki.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:03.500
Himena.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:05.140
Myself.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:06.280
Rei.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.000
Akari.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:09.210
Teruko.

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:13.380
And I suppose we're including Kunagisa as well.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:16.660
That makes seven.

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:25.620
Um, Hikari...

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:26.440
Yes?

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:31.880
When you took her the book at two, was
the storeroom window open? Or closed?

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.600
I think it was closed.

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:36.680
OK.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:40.100
That window's easily opened, right?

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:46.860
It was intended to air out the place...if you turn
the lever...like so...it opens and closes.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:52.100
But only from the inside. There's no way to open it from the outside.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:53.720
I see.

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:58.600
Um, Hikari...where is the room key kept?

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:02.640
Are we sure there's no spares anywhere?

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:09.880
I had the key on my person the whole time. There are
no spare keys, and the mansion has no master key.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:11.400
What kind of lock?

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:16.300
The normal kind. You turn it and the bolt slides home.

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:20.280
You're sure you locked it at two?

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:25.180
Yes. I'm sure I did. I checked several times to be sure.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:28.160
No question there.

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:30.040
I see.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:35.340
When you visited at two, was there anyone else in the room?

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:39.000
It was dark in there...could someone have been hiding?

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:41.760
I didn't notice anyone.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:47.760
But I can't say for sure. I didn't go in the room or anything.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.340
I just handed her the book at the door.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:53.520
Weren't you scared?

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:58.300
You knew that Sonoyama might have been the killer.

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:02.820
Meeting her in the middle of the night...weren't you scared?

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:06.080
No, I can't say that I was.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:10.500
I didn't think Sonoyama was the killer.

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:13.580
Why not? How can you say that?

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:15.580
Well...

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:23.580
But we can't really call it a locked room,
can we? I mean, the window was open.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:29.340
That alone defies the definition.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:32.360
But you can't get in and out of that window.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:37.260
There was a chair. If you stood on it...

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:39.260
You still couldn't reach it.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:42.800
Even if you reached out your hand and jumped.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:49.620
Shinya's the tallest person here, and I doubt even he could manage it.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:51.780
Interesting.

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:55.200
So the paint river made Ibuki's murder a locked room.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:56.210
2nd Floor, Ibuki Kanami's Room

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:59.960
And this time the height makes it a locked room.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:05.260
And both victims were beheaded.

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:11.760
Objectively speaking, Hikari is clearly the most suspicious.

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:14.300
Er, um, I...

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:18.600
Hikari had the key, and she's one of the three without an alibi.

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:24.980
If entry through the window was impossible,
then the only way in was through the door.

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:30.540
Three people have no alibi, but only you had the key.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:32.120
Wait a minute.

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:37.780
This is wrong. You can't just accuse someone like this.

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:41.500
Accuse? I am simply voicing what I have deduced.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:49.120
Choosing a criminal through selective thinking and
the process of elimination is...less than productive.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:53.960
Remember, it is easier to accuse than to be accused.

00:13:54.540 --> 00:14:00.760
Really? Is that so? I hardly see the problem with it.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:07.180
That kind of thinking led us to lock Akane
in the storeroom, as the prime suspect.

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:12.180
And what happened? This is the result, Ilia.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:17.520
I'm not making excuses for mistakes I've made...

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:21.620
But I at least need to avoid repeating them.

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:25.880
Understand me? Being alone put her in danger.

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:31.840
I don't see how that makes Hikari any less suspicious.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:34.360
Then how's this?

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:39.840
From this point on, being alone is too dangerous. Let us move in teams.

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:44.700
Since I've defended Hikari, I volunteer to be on a team with her.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.280
Kunagisa, Hikari and I are Team A.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.910
