00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:16.380
Alternatively, we could all remain in the
same room...like here, in the dining room.

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:18.480
Until Aikawa gets here.

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:24.220
If we all just stay still, none of us ever alone, nothing can happen.

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:29.240
Don't be absurd. Stay still? Out of the question.

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:33.280
Kunagisa and I have things to do.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:42.700
This is just...

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:45.560
Awful.

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:49.000
God! How could you let this happen!?

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:51.120
Too too too too too too too cruel!

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:55.760
Abuse! Devilry! There's a devil on this island! A diabolical one, Ii-chan!

00:15:55.760 --> 00:16:01.040
Tragedy is upon us! Augh! If this were a human
they'd have all organs pulped and all bones fractured!

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:03.140
Why would anyone do this?

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:05.840
Ohhh...the horror...

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:10.400
Ii-chan. Ii-chan Ii-chan Ii-chan, what is this!?

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:11.900
It's tragic.

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:17.160
But why? Who did it? The killer?

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:24.420
How obvious. Nice and simple.

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:28.740
Um, do you know why they did this?

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:35.500
Kunagisa took photographs of Kanami and
the studio, and moved them to her hard drive.

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:38.500
Guess the images she took were a problem.

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:47.760
I shouldn't have bothered protecting anything.
I never imagined anyone would resort to brute force!

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:50.700
There's no way to lock this room.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:53.080
Such bad luck.

00:16:53.500 --> 00:17:00.340
Sheesh. Now we can't stand around and wait for the detective to get here.

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:04.340
We've got to take action.

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:08.340
Hunh? Hang on a minute.

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:11.100
Who did this?

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:12.440
The killer.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.320
Although who that is...

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:21.500
But...we were all in the dining room. And then we came straight here.

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:26.080
Did any of us have time to stop and smash all these computers?

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.860
We'd been in the room until Akari arrived.

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:34.720
And we were the last to arrive at the scene of the crime.

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:39.160
When we got to the storeroom, everyone else had already arrived.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:43.500
Then everyone went straight to the dining room.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:45.740
If...

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:49.640
No, no ifs about it.

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:53.800
Logically, none of us could have carried out this destruction.

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:59.700
This is definitely the work of a human.

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:05.360
But if nobody could have done it...who did?

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:11.180
I didn't know. Yet another mystery.

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:15.500
Like Kanami's locked room and Akane's headless corpse.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.440
No, not like them.

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:22.920
The mystery here was nothing like the others.

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:28.240
The very nature of it was utterly unrelated
to nonsense like alibis and motives.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:32.700
This wasn't a trick or a gimmick...it was just impossible.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:35.260
In that case...

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:37.500
Is this the key?

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:40.220
If this is the key...

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:44.720
Then where is the door?

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:55.960
Where should we bury her, Hikari?

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:59.860
Definitely not by Ibuki's side...

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.120
That should do it.

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:20.200
Hikari, as long as we're outside anyway, can you
take us to see the storeroom window from the outside?

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.380
Sure, this way.

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:29.140
Thank you.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:36.220
You defended me this morning, didn't you? Thank you.

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:43.140
Oh...I wasn't really trying to defend you.
I just didn't want to make the same mistake.

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:48.680
Even if it wasn't a mistake, I...just don't like repetition.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:51.600
Especially at a time like this.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.580
So like you, Ii-chan!

00:19:54.580 --> 00:20:02.050
But you were defending Hikari, and you
know it! Hikari's your type with a capital T.

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:04.980
So what is my type, exactly?

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:16.150
Older, female, short, long hair, slender, no rings
or anything, and wearing an apron dress.

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:17.420
I deny the last one.

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:25.160
Or topless with jeans. Or wearing a white coat and glasses like a librarian.

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:29.280
Or taller delinquent girls with brown hair, wearing track suits.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:31.820
Must you reveal all my fetishes?

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:38.000
Well, I wanted to thank you.

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:42.680
Miss Ilia can be...rather a cold person sometimes.

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:51.880
And unlike the situation with Sonoyama, this time
even I can tell that I'm the only believable suspect.

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:55.340
No use going over that again, Hikari.

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:58.900
You've been polite to me.

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:02.700
Never lied to me. Kept your word.

00:21:03.520 --> 00:21:06.740
So...no need for gratitude.

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:07.980
But...

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:13.620
If our positions had been reversed,
would you have thrown me to the wolves?

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:18.140
No, you'd have done what you could to help me.

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:23.060
And then you would have thanked me for it.

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:27.060
See, we're friends, Hikari.

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:31.600
We don't doubt our friends.

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:36.900
So I know Ii-chan and Hikari can't be the killer.

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:38.680
Friends?

00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:43.060
I've never had any friends.

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:48.480
Ever since I can remember, I've been at Miss Ilia's side.

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:53.900
I've never had friends, either. Neither has Ii-chan.

00:21:56.680 --> 00:22:02.240
That's why I'm glad you're our friend, Hikari.

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:17.760
Realistically speaking, it'll be difficult for
Kunagisa and Hikari to remain friends.

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:24.140
Hikari will keep living on this island, by Ilia's side.

00:22:24.840 --> 00:22:27.800
While Kunagisa will be leaving soon.

00:22:28.520 --> 00:22:33.560
And once she does, Kunagisa will hole up in her apartment.

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:36.580
Kunagisa Tomo lives in isolation.

00:22:37.860 --> 00:22:38.700
And since I...

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:43.340
...can only see things in this light...

00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:46.020
...I'm even more isolated.

00:22:49.860 --> 00:22:52.220
Oh, here. That window.

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:54.960
Wait, you mean this?

00:22:54.960 --> 00:22:55.940
That's it!

00:22:55.940 --> 00:22:57.860
But...it's so low!

00:22:58.100 --> 00:23:04.760
It's high on the inside wall, but this side of
the mansion is half-buried in the mountain.

00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:10.560
That means it isn't very difficult to get inside.

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:14.260
But you can't open the window from outside.

00:23:14.920 --> 00:23:21.840
Then...is it possible Akane opened
the window herself, and let the killer in?

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:27.960
Someone knocked, she opened it. "Come on in!" Like so.

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:33.360
I doubt she'd be dumb enough to let the killer in, though.

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:36.100
I mean, this is Akane.

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:42.360
Even if Akane did invite the killer in, there's no way back out.

00:23:43.440 --> 00:23:48.860
Even a professional rock climber couldn't scramble up a perfectly flat wall.

00:23:49.040 --> 00:23:50.440
What if it was a gecko?

00:23:53.640 --> 00:23:55.720
Looks dangerous.

00:23:57.340 --> 00:24:01.540
Any ideas? Notice anything at all?

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:04.040
Not really.

00:24:04.780 --> 00:24:12.280
But if we assume they didn't come in the door, then
the killer must have come in through this window.

00:24:12.280 --> 00:24:13.520
Come in...?

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:18.220
Maybe they didn't come in at all.

00:24:18.980 --> 00:24:24.400
If the chair's right there, then Akane
must have been sitting on it, reading.

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:29.300
You could make a lasso or something, and lower it through the window.

00:24:29.860 --> 00:24:32.680
Get it caught around Akane's neck, and pull her up.

00:24:33.280 --> 00:24:38.340
Strangle her to death, pull her up to the window, and cut off her head.

00:24:38.860 --> 00:24:40.160
Does that work?

00:24:40.980 --> 00:24:42.680
No, not possible.

00:24:42.980 --> 00:24:47.700
Why? I thought it was a pretty good idea.

00:24:47.960 --> 00:24:51.080
Anyone could have done it, too.

00:24:51.420 --> 00:24:55.720
Human bodies aren't that light.

00:24:56.200 --> 00:24:59.880
The strongest of us...is probably Shinya, but...

00:25:00.680 --> 00:25:02.660
He's got an alibi.

00:25:01.220 --> 00:25:02.980
Let's try this shall
we just need a bit

00:25:01.220 --> 00:25:02.980
Blot some more crap
god damn I hate this
three whole lines of?

00:25:01.220 --> 00:25:02.980
<i>Sakaki Shinya</i>

00:25:01.220 --> 00:25:02.980
Before Earthquake     O

00:25:01.220 --> 00:25:02.980
After Earthquake       O

00:25:01.220 --> 00:25:02.980
(Ii-chan, Tomo, Maki, Hikari)

00:25:01.220 --> 00:25:02.980
(Maki)

00:25:03.340 --> 00:25:08.460
And I doubt even Shinya could pull someone up this high.

00:25:09.060 --> 00:25:11.140
Akane would have struggled, too.

00:25:11.760 --> 00:25:16.160
And even then, the window would have to be open.

00:25:16.640 --> 00:25:22.160
Akane would have to open it, and then
turn her back on the window, but...

00:25:22.600 --> 00:25:24.420
Does that seem likely?

00:25:24.780 --> 00:25:31.600
She's not an idiot. Quite intelligent, actually.
She'd have been on her guard.

00:25:33.620 --> 00:25:39.540
Here I thought I was getting a little
closer to the truth. But I was nowhere.

00:25:41.020 --> 00:25:42.920
Let's go back to the room.

00:25:51.320 --> 00:25:52.680
Anything?

00:25:53.060 --> 00:25:58.440
Nah, nothing. More importantly, Ii-chan, I'm hungry.

00:26:00.140 --> 00:26:00.920
Oh.

00:26:01.720 --> 00:26:03.920
Then let's eat lunch!

00:26:04.620 --> 00:26:05.600
Sounds good.

00:26:13.920 --> 00:26:19.390
The shape of the world I'd believed in

00:26:19.390 --> 00:26:22.810
Spun around when near you

00:26:22.970 --> 00:26:26.180
Leaning towards your right

00:26:26.180 --> 00:26:28.650
What I've got in my hands

00:26:28.650 --> 00:26:31.520
Is not a dream or nothing

00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:35.190
But there's something somewhere

00:26:35.190 --> 00:26:38.240
Throbbing in my heart

00:26:38.240 --> 00:26:41.160
If the one that you do love

00:26:41.160 --> 00:26:45.500
Agrees to put his arms around you

00:26:45.500 --> 00:26:48.250
Then what was a nebulous hope

00:26:48.250 --> 00:26:52.500
Shatters everything that kept you stable

00:26:52.500 --> 00:26:55.090
We'd once been so hollow

00:26:55.090 --> 00:26:57.920
Trapped inside that little box

00:26:57.920 --> 00:27:01.430
But now we've seen outside that box

00:27:01.430 --> 00:27:04.680
And have no idea where we are.

00:27:05.100 --> 00:27:06.520
That's all.

00:27:20.410 --> 00:27:22.910
Afterimages of our bliss

00:27:22.910 --> 00:27:25.740
Glimpses of the future

00:27:25.740 --> 00:27:29.330
A glance at something fragile

00:27:29.330 --> 00:27:34.170
Those times that we can still laugh together
